{
  "version": 1,
  "readme": [
    "ae-materials — struck discs solved from physics (Big Modal, manual ch. 30).",
    "",
    "Three `bigmodal` objects share lane 6: `drum` (mylar, even notes), `bell`",
    "(immortal glass, odd notes) and `plate` (anti-wood, notes divisible by 3).",
    "Each computes its sixteen modes from density, stiffness, radius, thickness",
    "and tension — `/drum` prints f1, the wave speed and f16/f1. The drum's strike",
    "point follows velocity; the bell morphs towards glass on a running chaotic",
    "orbit; an LFO slowly tightens the drum skin; a Lorenz orbit pushed by the",
    "drum's hits rotates where the plate is struck. Drum and bell also strike",
    "`atmo`, a Deep Pad tuned to G — one physical model playing another.",
    "",
    "Try:",
    "  /start",
    "  /drum                        the read-outs: f1 284Hz, c 1696m/s, f16/f1 4.85",
    "  /drum tension=0 2            a drum becomes a plate",
    "  /drum radius=40              halve the radius, watch f1 climb",
    "  /bell mat_b=rubber           morph towards something that doesn't ring",
    "  /plate mat_a=neutronium      the model gives up — a usable sound",
    "  /drum preset=kevlar_snare    load another factory object",
    "  /bell mod_morph=off          latch the bell: every hit a consistent object",
    "  /drum couple=0.8 grime=0.4 bite=0.7   make it behave like a thing"
  ],
